#NEXUS

[ pol2020a_fig3: Sauropodomorph time tree, read by eye from 3-6x crops (the lines are 2-3 px apart, too close for the line reader). The grey NHMUK PV R36834 and Barapasaurus are attached by short black stems to a node inside Eusauropoda; their dashed arrows show age uncertainty, not branches. Gravisauria and Eusauropoda, printed beside node dots, are kept as internal labels. Multi-way nodes: the Glacialisaurus-Coloradisaurus-Lufengosaurus node (entered at Coloradisaurus' height), the Massospondylus node, a six-way node (Melanorosaurus, Sefapanosaurus, Leonerasaurus, Aardonyx, the Lessemsaurus clade and the rest), the Lessemsaurus node, the Amygdalodon-Gongxianosaurus node, the NHMUK-Barapasaurus node and the Cetiosaurus node. Replacement for müller2020b_fig1 (seed 20261126). 46 tips, 7 polytomies (3, 3, 6, 3, 3, 3, 3 children); 2 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Random-sample case (seed 20261122). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

